      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we attempt to open the dev path if provided, and default to the bluetooth socket otherwise ? I think we should fail if the dev path does not point to a valid serial device.\n\nThe logic would be:\n```\nif (mDevPath.empty()) {\n   // No dev path provided, try opening the linux\n   // user Bluetooth channel.\n   mFd \u003d ..\n} else {\n   // Open the provided dev path.\n   mFd \u003d ..\n}\n\nif (mFd \u003d\u003d -1) {\n   ALOGD(\"Failed to configure Bluetooth HCI socket\");\n   return ndk::ScopedAStatus::fromServiceSpecificError(STATUS_BAD_VALUE);\n}\n```",
      "range": {
